warning[L0010]: sensitivity list leaves out `b`
  --> sensitivity.v:11:12
   |
11 |     always @(a) y = a & b;               // `b` is missing
   |            ^^^^
11 |     always @(a) y = a & b;               // `b` is missing
   |                         - read here
   |
   = note: use `always @*` so the list cannot go stale
   = note: lint: sensitivity-list, disable with `// reticle-lint: off sensitivity-list` or `(* lint_off = "sensitivity-list" *)`

warning[L0010]: sensitivity list mixes edge and level sensitivity
  --> sensitivity.v:13:29
   |
13 |     always @(posedge clk or b) z <= a;   // an edge next to a level
   |                             ^
13 |     always @(posedge clk or b) z <= a;   // an edge next to a level
   |            ------------------- in this list
   |
   = note: an edge-triggered block must list only edges
   = note: lint: sensitivity-list, disable with `// reticle-lint: off sensitivity-list` or `(* lint_off = "sensitivity-list" *)`

warning[L0010]: `always @*` reads nothing
  --> sensitivity.v:15:12
   |
15 |     always @* w = 1'b0;                  // reads nothing at all
   |            ^^
   |
   = note: the block will never run again after time zero
   = note: lint: sensitivity-list, disable with `// reticle-lint: off sensitivity-list` or `(* lint_off = "sensitivity-list" *)`

